{
  "name": "green iguana",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/herps/iguana.py): the GREEN IGUANA, Iguana iguana, 1.5 m long, the tail two thirds of it. A deep box-like head, the crown flat, the snout long, blunt and planed at the sides, a clear brow ridge over the eye, heavy jowls; the big round SUBTYMPANIC SHIELD on the cheek below the eardrum (a pale raised disc); a large DEWLAP on the throat's midline from the chin to the chest (a `fin`, thicker at its root, its rim one convex arc, the throat's scales, a darker rim); a CREST of soft spines from the nape down the back (serrated `fin`s, one per bone, tallest on the neck) going on as a low comb down the first half of the tail; conical tubercles on the neck's sides; a trunk a little deeper than wide on strong sprawled legs; long toes (the hind 4th the longest) with sharp curved claws (`horn`s); the tail long and whip-like, flattened a little side to side, tapering to a point (one `sweep` along caud1..4), ringed dark (its `bands`). Small bead scales (`scales`). Coats: GREEN (base, faint dark bars on the flanks), the ORANGE breeding male; variant `juvenile` (.3, bright green). A slow sprawling walk, the trunk and tail swinging.",
  "kind": "parts",
